                        "sense_id": "02266b9d-8183-376c-bd5b-078639d654b2",
                        "entry_id": "6d0b52f0-563e-3fd5-931d-b5e1939639ad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to Antichrist."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b4d0157-48ff-45d1-a874-6193d2311530",
                                "sense_id": "02266b9d-8183-376c-bd5b-078639d654b2",
                                "text": "it was first establisht and put in practice by Antichristian malice and mystery on set purpose to extinguish, if it were possible, the light of Reformation, and to settle falshood; little differing from that policie wherewith the Turk upholds his Alcoran, by the prohibition of Printing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5db9f13a-6797-49f3-a6ad-e169e3c6fe20",
                                "sense_id": "02266b9d-8183-376c-bd5b-078639d654b2",
                                "text": "They gave their power and authority to the beast—lent themselves to the support of the antichristian usurpation; prompted to this partly by superstitious reverence for the spiritual authority it claimed, and partly, perhaps chiefly, by political aims and exigencies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e334b5a-5430-4dea-a359-93aab1fefe47",
                                "sense_id": "02266b9d-8183-376c-bd5b-078639d654b2",
                                "text": "To oppose the gathering of churches was described as siding with Antichrist in a pamphlet of 1644. Separation from an antichristian church was permissible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23111384-fe14-4ebc-be71-7c905aaca78b",
                                "sense_id": "02266b9d-8183-376c-bd5b-078639d654b2",
                                "text": "Thus Articles 78 and 80, which unequivocally asserted the pope's antichristian nature, were among the Irish Articles revoked in 1634."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
